<map version="1.0.1">
<node ID="ID_394" TEXT="Chapter 0 — Setup, accounts and the eligibility gate"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>2026-09-05 → 2026-09-06</p><p>Getting ready</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_246" TEXT="🎯 Goal"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Everything administrative is out of the way so that from Chapter 1 every session is pure learning.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_290" TEXT="📅 Daily plan"><node ID="ID_258" TEXT="09-05 · Partner Academy account with your UST email (amit.phadke@ust.com); …"><node ID="ID_247" TEXT="Learn: Partner Academy account with your UST email (amit.phadke@ust.com); download the official Exam Guide PDF"></node><node ID="ID_252" TEXT="Build: Copy the 8 domain weights into your notes"><node ID="ID_248" TEXT="Register with your UST email amit.phadke@ust.com (partner-organisation status unlocks the exam guide and the free prep course — if UST is not listed as a partner, register anyway and use the public Claude Academy course instead)."></node><node ID="ID_249" TEXT="Download the Exam Guide PDF and store it in the lab repo under docs/."></node><node ID="ID_250" TEXT="Copy the domain table into notes/00-exam-guide.md: domain, weight, and the task statements under each."></node><node ID="ID_251" TEXT="Highlight every verb in the task statements (&quot;select&quot;, &quot;implement&quot;, &quot;troubleshoot&quot;) — these tell you how questions are framed."></node></node><node ID="ID_253" TEXT="✔ Done when: notes/00-exam-guide.md exists with all 8 domains, their weights and task statements."></node><node ID="ID_257" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_254" TEXT="Official CCDV-F Exam Guide (Anthropic PDF)" LINK="https://everpath-course-content.s3-accelerate.amazonaws.com/instructor%2F6nizmqk8tpzpfjvt6qmmav7rh%2Fpublic%2F1783542875%2FClaude+Certified+Developer+%E2%80%93+Foundations+Exam+Guide.pdf"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://everpath-course-content.s3-accelerate.amazonaws.com/instructor%2F6nizmqk8tpzpfjvt6qmmav7rh%2Fpublic%2F1783542875%2FClaude+Certified+Developer+%E2%80%93+Foundations+Exam+Guide.pdf</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_255" TEXT="Partner Academy — register and find the prep course" LINK="https://anthropic-partners.skilljar.com"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://anthropic-partners.skilljar.com</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_256" TEXT="Community blueprint page (weights, sub-skills)" LINK="https://claudecertificationguide.com/ccdv-f"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://claudecertificationguide.com/ccdv-f</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_269" TEXT="09-05 · Claude Console: create API key, load $10–20 credit, find the usage …"><node ID="ID_259" TEXT="Learn: Claude Console: create API key, load $10–20 credit, find the usage dashboard"></node><node ID="ID_264" TEXT="Build: Store key in .env, never commit"><node ID="ID_260" TEXT="Create an organisation and a workspace named ccdvf-lab so spend is isolated."></node><node ID="ID_261" TEXT="Create one API key; name it by machine (macbook-air) so you can revoke it later."></node><node ID="ID_262" TEXT="Add $10–20 of credit; set a monthly spend limit on the workspace."></node><node ID="ID_263" TEXT="Open Usage and Cost pages — note where per-model token counts appear; you will reconcile against them in Chapter 2."></node></node><node ID="ID_265" TEXT="✔ Done when: Key in .env, .env in .gitignore, spend limit set, you can point at the usage dashboard."></node><node ID="ID_268" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_266" TEXT="Claude Console" LINK="https://platform.claude.com"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://platform.claude.com</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_267" TEXT="API getting started" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/api/overview"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/api/overview</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_279" TEXT="09-06 · Local lab: git repo, Python venv, pip install anthropic mcp python-…"><node ID="ID_270" TEXT="Learn: Local lab: git repo, Python venv, pip install anthropic mcp python-dotenv"></node><node ID="ID_275" TEXT="Build: hello.py — first client.messages.create() call"><node ID="ID_271" TEXT="mkdir ccdvf-lab &amp;&amp; git init; python3 -m venv .venv &amp;&amp; source .venv/bin/activate"></node><node ID="ID_272" TEXT="pip install anthropic mcp python-dotenv pytest; pip freeze &gt; requirements.txt"></node><node ID="ID_273" TEXT="Write hello.py: load .env, create Anthropic(), send one message, print response.content[0].text, stop_reason and usage."></node><node ID="ID_274" TEXT="Commit. Open the repo in Claude Code (claude) and ask it to add a README describing the lab layout."></node></node><node ID="ID_276" TEXT="✔ Done when: hello.py prints a reply plus stop_reason=end_turn and a usage object; first commit pushed."></node><node ID="ID_278" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_277" TEXT="Python SDK quickstart" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/api/client-sdks"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/api/client-sdks</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_289" TEXT="09-06 · Confirm Pearson VUE booking details: name matches ID, phone is +91,…"><node ID="ID_280" TEXT="Learn: Confirm Pearson VUE booking details: name matches ID, phone is +91, run OnVUE system test"></node><node ID="ID_285" TEXT="Build: Screenshot the confirmation"><node ID="ID_281" TEXT="Log in to Pearson VUE; open the appointment; check the candidate name is exactly as printed on the ID you will show."></node><node ID="ID_282" TEXT="Correct the phone number to +91 format."></node><node ID="ID_283" TEXT="Run the OnVUE system test on the same laptop, same room, same network you will use on exam day."></node><node ID="ID_284" TEXT="Save the confirmation email as PDF into docs/ and note the check-in link."></node></node><node ID="ID_286" TEXT="✔ Done when: System test passed; confirmation screenshot saved; name and phone verified."></node><node ID="ID_288" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_287" TEXT="Pearson VUE — Anthropic testing" LINK="https://www.pearsonvue.com/us/en/anthropic.html"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://www.pearsonvue.com/us/en/anthropic.html</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node></node><node ID="ID_324" TEXT="📖 Study material"><node ID="ID_297" TEXT="Exam facts"><node ID="ID_291" TEXT="53 questions, multiple-choice and multiple-response (each item says how many to…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>53 questions, multiple-choice and multiple-response (each item says how many to select). Scenario-heavy: most stems describe a situation and ask for the best next step.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_292" TEXT="120 minutes of exam time; the 135-minute booking includes NDA and tutorial."></node><node ID="ID_293" TEXT="Pass = 720 scaled on a 100–1000 scale (not a raw 72%). Scaling means some items count…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Pass = 720 scaled on a 100–1000 scale (not a raw 72%). Scaling means some items count more than others; you cannot game it, so aim for 80%+ on practice.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_294" TEXT="USD 125 per attempt; credential valid 12 months. Retake waits: 14 days after the 1st…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>USD 125 per attempt; credential valid 12 months. Retake waits: 14 days after the 1st fail, 30 after the 2nd, 90 after the 3rd; maximum four attempts in a rolling 12 months.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_295" TEXT="Reschedule or cancel at least 24 hours before the appointment. Renewal is a free,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Reschedule or cancel at least 24 hours before the appointment. Renewal is a free, non-proctored Partner Academy assessment; a lapsed credential means a full retake.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_296" TEXT="Target audience per the guide: 1–5 years software experience, 6+ months hands-on…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Target audience per the guide: 1–5 years software experience, 6+ months hands-on Claude, Python/TypeScript, REST, CLI, MCP — i.e. it tests engineering judgement as much as API trivia.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_310" TEXT="Domain weights and sub-skills (from the official exam guide)"><node ID="ID_298" TEXT="Applications &amp; Integration"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>33.1% · 17–18 · Understanding Requirements 3.4 · Systems Life Cycle 2.8 · Claude API Mechanics 6.8 · Software Engineering Foundations 7.4 · Claude Application Design 8.6 · Configuration Management 4.1 · Ch 1, 2 + Library gap entries</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_299" TEXT="Model Selection &amp; Optimisation"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>16.8% · 9 · LLM Fundamentals 5.2 · Technical Fundamentals (SDK integration, websockets) 6.1 · Model Selection &amp; Trade-offs 2.7 · Cost &amp; Token Management 2.8 · Ch 3</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_300" TEXT="Agents &amp; Workflows"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>14.7% · 8 · Agent Architecture 4.5 · Agent Construction (Agent SDK, custom loops, deployment) 5.3 · Agent Patterns (LangGraph etc., memory) 4.9 · Ch 4</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_301" TEXT="Prompt &amp; Context Engineering"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>11.0% · 6 · Context Engineering 3.8 · Prompt Engineering 4.6 · Output Handling (structured output, validation, defensive parsing) 2.6 · Ch 3</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_302" TEXT="Tools &amp; MCPs"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>10.6% · 5–6 · Tool Implementation 4.4 · MCP Server Development 2.1 · Agentic Customization (tools vs Skills vs MCP) 4.1 · Ch 2, 5</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_303" TEXT="Security &amp; Safety"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>8.1% · 4 · AI Application Security 3.2 · Guardrails &amp; Safe Deployment 2.3 · Claude Hooks 1.0 · Identity &amp; Secrets 1.6 · Ch 7 (+6)</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_304" TEXT="Claude Code"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>3.1% · 1–2 · Rules, Skills, Commands, Agents, Agent Memory; sessions, slash commands, headless/streaming · Ch 6</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_305" TEXT="Eval, Testing &amp; Debugging"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>2.6% · 1–2 · Error identification, recovery strategies, trace analysis · Ch 7</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_309" TEXT="💡 Tip"><node ID="ID_306" TEXT="Effort allocation: Chapters 1–3 cover about 61% of the exam."></node><node ID="ID_307" TEXT="If you fall behind, protect those and compress Chapter 6 (Claude Code is ~2 questions, and you use it daily)."></node><node ID="ID_308" TEXT="Note that roughly 22 points of the biggest domain are general engineering (requirements, life cycle, SE foundations, application design) — the five &quot;blueprint gap&quot; entries in the Library cover them; read them in Chapters 1 and 3."></node></node></node><node ID="ID_315" TEXT="The three official sample questions"><node ID="ID_311" TEXT="Domain 2 — 10,000 documents to process overnight cost-effectively → Message Batches…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Domain 2 — 10,000 documents to process overnight cost-effectively → Message Batches API (asynchronous, within 24 h, reduced cost).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_312" TEXT="Domain 7 — hidden text in a document tries to redirect the model → treat content as…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Domain 7 — hidden text in a document tries to redirect the model → treat content as untrusted, isolate it from trusted instructions, use guardrails/hooks.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_313" TEXT="Domain 8 — make an inventory REST API reusable across several apps → build an MCP…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Domain 8 — make an inventory REST API reusable across several apps → build an MCP server exposing the operations as tools.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_314" TEXT="Pattern: every sample rewards the Anthropic-recommended architecture, not the…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Pattern: every sample rewards the Anthropic-recommended architecture, not the cleverest one.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_321" TEXT="Daily routine (1.5 h)"><node ID="ID_316" TEXT="45 min learn from the docs or course → 45 min build the day's lab. Each day below has…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>45 min learn from the docs or course → 45 min build the day's lab. Each day below has a Read list, numbered Steps and a Done when line — tick the day only when that line is true.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_317" TEXT="Build every lab with Claude Code, not by hand — end each session with /cost and note…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Build every lab with Claude Code, not by hand — end each session with /cost and note tokens used.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_318" TEXT="Keep one notes/&lt;domain&gt;.md per chapter; it becomes your revision sheet in Chapter 8."></node><node ID="ID_319" TEXT="Sunday = review day: finish the notes file, do the chapter Self-check, take the domain…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Sunday = review day: finish the notes file, do the chapter Self-check, take the domain quiz in the Question bank tab, fill the Weekly retrospective.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_320" TEXT="Every day, before anything else: open the Trap review tab and clear what is due (2–5…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Every day, before anything else: open the Trap review tab and clear what is due (2–5 minutes).</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_323" TEXT="Lab repo layout"><node ID="ID_322" TEXT="{ } code sample"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>ccdvf-lab/</p><p>  .env                # ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...  (git-ignored)</p><p>  CLAUDE.md           # written properly in Chapter 6</p><p>  docs/               # exam guide, confirmation</p><p>  notes/              # one .md per chapter → cheat sheet</p><p>  ch1/ ch2/ ... ch7/  # one folder per chapter's scripts</p><p>  evals/              # Chapter 7</p><p>  mcp_server/         # Chapter 5</p><p>  tests/</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_365" TEXT="📚 Library digests"><node ID="ID_345" TEXT="Official CCDV-F Exam Guide (Anthropic)" LINK="https://everpath-course-content.s3-accelerate.amazonaws.com/instructor%2F6nizmqk8tpzpfjvt6qmmav7rh%2Fpublic%2F1783542875%2FClaude+Certified+Developer+%E2%80%93+Foundations+Exam+Guide.pdf"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://everpath-course-content.s3-accelerate.amazonaws.com/instructor%2F6nizmqk8tpzpfjvt6qmmav7rh%2Fpublic%2F1783542875%2FClaude+Certified+Developer+%E2%80%93+Foundations+Exam+Guide.pdf</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_340" TEXT="Key facts"><node ID="ID_325" TEXT="Credential: Claude Certified Developer – Foundations, code CCDV-F. 53 items (multiple-choice and…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Credential: Claude Certified Developer – Foundations, code CCDV-F. 53 items (multiple-choice and multiple-response), 120 minutes, proctored online or test centre, pass 720 on a 100–1,000 scale, USD 125, valid 12 months from award.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_326" TEXT="Target audience: technical professionals who build, integrate and ship production-grade AI…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Target audience: technical professionals who build, integrate and ship production-grade AI solutions; 1–5 years software experience, 6+ months hands-on Claude/LLM experience, Python and/or TypeScript, REST APIs, CLI tools, LLM fundamentals, agents, context management, MCP. No mandatory prerequisites.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_327" TEXT="Domain 1 Agents and Workflows 14.7%: Agent Architecture 4.5% (patterns, manager hierarchies,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Domain 1 Agents and Workflows 14.7%: Agent Architecture 4.5% (patterns, manager hierarchies, workflow-vs-agent decisions); Agent Construction 5.3% (Claude Agent SDK, custom loops, deployment models); Agent Patterns 4.9% (design patterns, frameworks such as LangGraph, memory management).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_328" TEXT="Domain 2 Applications and Integration 33.1%: Understanding Requirements 3.4%; Systems Life Cycle…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Domain 2 Applications and Integration 33.1%: Understanding Requirements 3.4%; Systems Life Cycle 2.8%; Claude API Mechanics 6.8% (messages, tools, streaming, vision, caching, batch); Software Engineering Foundations 7.4% (REST APIs, JSON, version control, refactoring); Claude Application Design 8.6% (interface interpretation, schema design, session hygiene); Configuration Management 4.1% (CLAUDE.md, settings.json, model versioning).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_329" TEXT="Domain 3 Claude Code 3.1%: core components — rules, skills, commands, agents, agent memory;…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Domain 3 Claude Code 3.1%: core components — rules, skills, commands, agents, agent memory; features — session management, slash commands, headless/streaming modes.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_330" TEXT="Domain 4 Eval, Testing and Debugging 2.6%: error identification, recovery strategies, trace…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Domain 4 Eval, Testing and Debugging 2.6%: error identification, recovery strategies, trace analysis for failure modes.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_331" TEXT="Domain 5 Model Selection and Optimization 16.8%: LLM Fundamentals 5.2% (tokens, context windows,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Domain 5 Model Selection and Optimization 16.8%: LLM Fundamentals 5.2% (tokens, context windows, sampling, prompting techniques); Technical Fundamentals 6.1% (SDK integration, websockets); Model Selection and Trade-offs 2.7% (Opus/Sonnet/Haiku, quality vs latency vs cost); Cost and Token Management 2.8% (token tracking, caching strategies).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_332" TEXT="Domain 6 Prompt and Context Engineering 11.0%: Context Engineering 3.8% (context drift…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Domain 6 Prompt and Context Engineering 11.0%: Context Engineering 3.8% (context drift prevention, subagent isolation); Prompt Engineering 4.6% (instruction clarity, few-shot, iterative refinement); Output Handling 2.6% (structured output, validation, defensive parsing).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_333" TEXT="Domain 7 Security and Safety 8.1%: AI Application Security 3.2% (prompt injection, jailbreak…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Domain 7 Security and Safety 8.1%: AI Application Security 3.2% (prompt injection, jailbreak defence, PII); Guardrails and Safe Deployment 2.3% (content policy, secure-by-design); Claude Hooks 1.0% (guardrails preventing destructive actions); Identity and Secrets Management 1.6%.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_334" TEXT="Domain 8 Tools and MCPs 10.6%: Tool Implementation 4.4% (function calling, tool descriptions,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Domain 8 Tools and MCPs 10.6%: Tool Implementation 4.4% (function calling, tool descriptions, agentic patterns); MCP Server Development 2.1% (authoring, deployment, communication patterns); Agentic Customization 4.1% (trade-offs among tools, Skills and MCPs).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_335" TEXT="Preparation: self-assess against the blueprint; review official docs (API, models, prompt…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Preparation: self-assess against the blueprint; review official docs (API, models, prompt engineering, Claude Code, Skills, MCP); build and operate a real Claude application with tools, prompt/context engineering and security practices; practise prompts, agents, Claude Code configuration, token management, guardrails, custom tools/MCPs; study the sample questions.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_336" TEXT="Sample 1 (Domain 2): 10,000 documents overnight, cost-effectively → Message Batches API…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Sample 1 (Domain 2): 10,000 documents overnight, cost-effectively → Message Batches API (asynchronous, within 24 h, reduced cost). Sample 2 (Domain 7): hidden prompt-injection text → treat content as untrusted, isolate from trusted instructions, use guardrails/hooks. Sample 3 (Domain 8): make an inventory REST API reusable across apps → build an MCP server exposing the operations as tools.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_337" TEXT="Retakes: wait 14 days after the 1st fail, 30 days after the 2nd, 90 days after the 3rd; maximum…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Retakes: wait 14 days after the 1st fail, 30 days after the 2nd, 90 days after the 3rd; maximum four attempts in a rolling 12 months; USD 125 per attempt.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_338" TEXT="Conduct: valid government photo ID with name matching registration; no phones, notes, second…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Conduct: valid government photo ID with name matching registration; no phones, notes, second monitors or recording; stay in webcam view; 24-hour cancellation/reschedule deadline; confidentiality agreement before the exam; cheating or content disclosure = invalidation, revocation and ban.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_339" TEXT="Maintenance: renewal is a free, non-proctored assessment on the Partner Academy covering changes…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Maintenance: renewal is a free, non-proctored assessment on the Partner Academy covering changes since certification; a lapsed credential needs a full retake at full fee. Name corrections: certifications-support@anthropic.com; scheduling/accommodations/results: Pearson VUE; appeals within 14 days.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_344" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_341" TEXT="The 24-hour reschedule deadline is the real go/no-go cut-off — decide by the morning of 2 Nov at the latest, not on 3 Nov."></node><node ID="ID_342" TEXT="Second and third fails cost 30 and 90 days of waiting — the first attempt is the cheap one to get right."></node><node ID="ID_343" TEXT="Roughly a quarter of the exam (Requirements, Life Cycle, SE Foundations, App Design) is general engineering judgement, not Claude API trivia."></node></node></node><node ID="ID_356" TEXT="Courses: Claude Academy, Partner Academy, Skilljar MCP course, cookbook" LINK="https://academy.claude.com"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://academy.claude.com</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_352" TEXT="Key facts"><node ID="ID_346" TEXT="Claude Academy (academy.claude.com): free video courses with quizzes — 'Claude Platform 101'…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Claude Academy (academy.claude.com): free video courses with quizzes — 'Claude Platform 101' (models, console, pricing, prompting basics) and 'Building with the Claude API' (messages, streaming, tools, caching, batches, vision, evals). Run every sample in your own lab instead of the notebook.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_347" TEXT="Partner Academy (anthropic-partners.skilljar.com): partner-organisation portal — exam guide,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Partner Academy (anthropic-partners.skilljar.com): partner-organisation portal — exam guide, official CCDV-F prep course and quizzes, renewal assessment. Register with your UST email; if UST is not a listed partner, fall back to the public Academy.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_348" TEXT="Introduction to MCP (anthropic.skilljar.com): architecture, primitives, building a server with…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Introduction to MCP (anthropic.skilljar.com): architecture, primitives, building a server with the Python SDK, Inspector, connecting to Claude Desktop/Code.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_349" TEXT="GitHub: anthropics/courses (API fundamentals, prompt engineering, tool use, evaluations…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>GitHub: anthropics/courses (API fundamentals, prompt engineering, tool use, evaluations notebooks); anthropic-cookbook patterns/agents (chaining, routing, parallelisation, orchestrator, evaluator code); prompt-eng-interactive-tutorial (9 chapters with exercises).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_350" TEXT="Console (platform.claude.com): Workbench (prompt generator/improver, compare runs), Usage and…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Console (platform.claude.com): Workbench (prompt generator/improver, compare runs), Usage and Cost pages (per model, per key), spend limits, API keys, workspaces.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_351" TEXT="Community: claudecertificationguide.com (blueprint mirror, free practice questions); Udemy…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Community: claudecertificationguide.com (blueprint mirror, free practice questions); Udemy practice tests (optional, quality varies — treat as timing practice, verify answers against the docs).</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_355" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_353" TEXT="Official prep = Partner Academy course + docs; community practice sets are for timing, not truth."></node><node ID="ID_354" TEXT="Run the course code in your lab with /cost open — the exam asks about token/cost behaviour you only notice by measuring."></node></node></node><node ID="ID_364" TEXT="Pearson VUE / OnVUE logistics" LINK="https://www.pearsonvue.com/us/en/anthropic.html"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://www.pearsonvue.com/us/en/anthropic.html</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_360" TEXT="Key facts"><node ID="ID_357" TEXT="Booking: name on the Pearson VUE profile must match the government photo ID exactly; keep the…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Booking: name on the Pearson VUE profile must match the government photo ID exactly; keep the phone in +91 format; confirmation email carries the check-in link.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_358" TEXT="OnVUE (online proctored): run the system test on the same laptop, room and network you will use;…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>OnVUE (online proctored): run the system test on the same laptop, room and network you will use; install the OnVUE app the day before; check-in opens 30 minutes before (10:00 IST for a 10:30 start) — photo of ID, room scan, no second monitor, phone out of reach, nobody enters the room.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_359" TEXT="Reschedule/cancel at least 24 hours before the appointment (per the exam guide); Pearson VUE…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Reschedule/cancel at least 24 hours before the appointment (per the exam guide); Pearson VUE support handles scheduling, accommodations and results; appeals within 14 days.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_363" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_361" TEXT="Decide go/no-go by the morning of 2 Nov — the 24-hour window is the hard line."></node><node ID="ID_362" TEXT="Same laptop + same room + same network for the system test and the exam."></node></node></node></node><node ID="ID_374" TEXT="❓ Self-check"><node ID="ID_367" TEXT="What is the passing score and how is it expressed?"><node ID="ID_366" TEXT="→ 720 on a scaled 100–1000 range — a scaled score, not a raw percentage."></node></node><node ID="ID_369" TEXT="How many questions and how long?"><node ID="ID_368" TEXT="→ 53 questions in 120 minutes; the booking is 135 minutes including NDA and tutorial."></node></node><node ID="ID_371" TEXT="Which two domains together are roughly half the exam?"><node ID="ID_370" TEXT="→ Applications &amp; Integration (33.1%) and Model Selection &amp; Optimisation (16.8%)."></node></node><node ID="ID_373" TEXT="How long is the credential valid and what is the retake wait?"><node ID="ID_372" TEXT="→ 12 months; 14 days after a failed attempt."></node></node></node><node ID="ID_381" TEXT="⚠ Traps to drill"><node ID="ID_376" TEXT="The pass mark is 720 — is that 72% of questions right?"><node ID="ID_375" TEXT="→ No. 720 is a scaled score on 100–1000; raw percentage needed is unknown, so target 80%+ on practice exams."></node></node><node ID="ID_378" TEXT="Retake waits after a 1st, 2nd, 3rd fail?"><node ID="ID_377" TEXT="→ 14, 30, 90 days; max four attempts in a rolling 12 months; USD 125 each. Reschedule ≥24 h before."></node></node><node ID="ID_380" TEXT="Which domain deserves the most study time?"><node ID="ID_379" TEXT="→ Applications &amp; Integration at 33.1% — Messages API, tools, caching, batches, streaming, errors."></node></node></node><node ID="ID_385" TEXT="🗒 Cheat sheet"><node ID="ID_382" TEXT="53 Qs · 120 min · pass 720/1000 scaled · valid 12 months · USD 125 · retakes 14/30/90 days, max 4 in 12 months · reschedule ≥24 h before"></node><node ID="ID_383" TEXT="Weights: AI 33.1 · MSO 16.8 · AW 14.7 · PCE 11.0 · TM 10.6 · SS 8.1 · CC 3.1 · ETD 2.6"></node><node ID="ID_384" TEXT="Check-in 10:00 IST, start 10:30 IST, Tue 3 Nov 2026 — ID on desk, phone away, single monitor"></node></node><node ID="ID_393" TEXT="☑ Chapter checklist"><node ID="ID_386" TEXT="Exam registered and paid (Tue 3 Nov 2026, 10:30 IST)"></node><node ID="ID_387" TEXT="Pearson VUE profile: name exactly as on ID, phone corrected to +91"></node><node ID="ID_388" TEXT="OnVUE system test passed on the laptop you will use"></node><node ID="ID_389" TEXT="Claude Console API key working (hello.py returned a response)"></node><node ID="ID_390" TEXT="Lab repo created on GitHub with .gitignore for .env"></node><node ID="ID_391" TEXT="Claude Code installed and logged in (claude --version)"></node><node ID="ID_392" TEXT="Bookmarked: docs.claude.com, academy.claude.com, Partner Academy"></node></node></node>
